      "text": [
        " فِي كِتَابِ عَلِيٍّ ( عليه السلام ) إِذَا طَرَفَتِ الْعَيْنُ أَوْ رَكَضَتِ الرِّجْلُ أَوْ تَحَرَّكَ الذَّنَبُ فَكُلْ مِنْهُ فَقَدْ أَدْرَكْتَ ذَكَاتَهُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Al Husayn Bin Muhammad, from Moala Bin Muhammad, from Al Washa, from Aban, from Abdul Rahman Bin Abu Abdullah, ",
          "Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> has said: ‘In the Book of Ali<sup>asws</sup> (it is written): ‘When the eye is blinking, or the feet are kicking, or the tail is moving, so eat from it, for you have realised its slaughter’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Al-Husayn from Muhammad has narrated from Mu‘alla’ ibn Muhammad from Aban from ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn abu ‘Abd Allah who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said that it is in the book of Ali, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, that if the eye turns or the leg runs or the tail moves, then slaughtering properly is achieved.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
